        "original_id": "609bcc65-8361-566e-ba97-ee0c3d3531ee",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eric Clapton, Bobby Whitlock, Carl Radle, Jim Gordon\n- Bands: Derek and the Dominos, Delaney & Bonnie and Friends, Blind Faith\n- Albums: E. C. Was Here, In Concert\n- Places: Long Beach Arena, Hammersmith Odeon, Providence Civic Center\n- Organizations: Record Plant Remote\n- Events: Derek and the Dominos' formation, Clapton's 1974–1975 tour\n\nFacts:\n- In the spring of 1970, Eric Clapton, Bobby Whitlock, Carl Radle, and Jim Gordon formed the blues rock band Derek and the Dominos.\n- Before Derek and the Dominos formed, all four members had played together in Delaney & Bonnie and Friends during and after Eric Clapton's brief tenure with Blind Faith.\n- Eric Clapton's first tour since Derek and the Dominos in 1970 took place in 1974 and 1975.\n- The live album E. C. Was Here was recorded during Eric Clapton's 1974 and 1975 tour at the Long Beach Arena, the Hammersmith Odeon, and the Providence Civic Center.\n- Record Plant Remote recorded E. C. Was Here live during Eric Clapton's 1974 and 1975 tour.\n- Eric Clapton's 1974 and 1975 tour resulted in the album In Concert.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "8a8f254e-0ae0-53a9-a8c8-232d81802894",
        "text": "Page: E. C. Was Here. Sentence: It was recorded live in 1974 and 1975 at the Long Beach Arena, the Hammersmith Odeon, and the Providence Civic Center by Record Plant Remote during Clapton's first tour since Derek and the Dominos in 1970, which resulted in the \"In Concert\" album.\nPage: Derek and the Dominos. Sentence: Derek and the Dominos were a blues rock band formed in the spring of 1970 by guitarist and singer Eric Clapton, keyboardist and singer Bobby Whitlock, bassist Carl Radle and drummer Jim Gordon.\nPage: Derek and the Dominos. Sentence: All four members had previously played together in Delaney & Bonnie and Friends, during and after Clapton's brief tenure with Blind Faith.",
